---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ResearchTheme from '../../components/ResearchTheme.astro';
import { researchThemes } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Research" description="Research directions and selected public work by Shivam Pandey across embodied intelligence, world models, interpretability, and AI systems.">
  <header class="page-head shell">
    <p class="section-index">01 / Research</p>
    <h1>Questions that cross<br/><em>the stack.</em></h1>
    <p>I work where learning signals, representations, action, and compute meet. The programme below separates active research directions from established technical practice.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="theme-grid shell" aria-label="Research themes">
    {researchThemes.map((theme) => <ResearchTheme {...theme} />)}
  </section>

  <section class="research-note shell">
    <p class="section-index">02 / Current focus</p>
    <div>
      <h2>Alignment becomes concrete when a model can act.</h2>
      <p>My current direction asks how learned world representations, training signals, and policies interact in embodied settings. The emphasis is diagnostic: identify what a policy uses, where behaviour changes, and which scenarios expose the difference between the intended objective and the learned one.</p>
      <p class="status-note"><span>Ongoing investigation</span> This is a research direction, not a claim of completed results or publication.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
